<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Kotor Old Town Walking Tour - Kim and Dave</name><Placemark><name>0. Start: Sea Gate (Main Gate)</name><description>Main entrance to the Old Town, on the water side. Built 1555. Taxis and coaches drop nearby; the cruise pier is across the road.</description><Point><coordinates>18.769704,42.424737,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1. Square of Arms &amp; Clock Tower</name><description>The big square just inside the gate. Clock Tower begun 1602, pillory at its foot; Rector's Palace and the 1810 theatre along the wall.</description><Point><coordinates>18.770057,42.424842,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1a. Pima Palace, Square of Flour (pass-by)</name><description>On the way from the Clock Tower to the Cathedral.</description><Point><coordinates>18.770776,42.424283,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Cathedral of St Tryphon</name><description>Pin is on the cathedral square in front of the two bell towers. Consecrated 1166. Small ticket.</description><Point><coordinates>18.771207,42.424309,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Maritime Museum (Grgurina Palace)</name><description>A minute north of the cathedral. Small ticket.</description><Point><coordinates>18.771401,42.425048,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4a. Church of St Luke</name><description>St Luke's Square. Built 1195; Catholic and Orthodox altars 1657-1812.</description><Point><coordinates>18.771213,42.425504,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4b. Church of St Nicholas</name><description>Serbian Orthodox, 1902-1909, two bell towers with black domes.</description><Point><coordinates>18.77089,42.425815,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. River Gate (North Gate) &amp; Bembo Bastion</name><description>North gate on the Škurda river, 1540.</description><Point><coordinates>18.772159,42.426251,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6. Fortress climb entrance (north ticket gate) - optional</name><description>Start of the climb to the Fortress of St John. About 1,350 steps, little shade.</description><Point><coordinates>18.772868,42.425743,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6a. Our Lady of Remedy (turnaround point)</name><description>Church of 1518 partway up the climb. Good view for much less effort.</description><Point><coordinates>18.773259,42.424271,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6b. Fortress of St John (top)</name><description>About 260-280 m above the sea.</description><Point><coordinates>18.774847,42.422096,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>
